      "text": "To determine the values of \\( m \\) and \\( b \\) such that the lines intersect at the point \\((6, 10)\\), we start by substituting \\( x = 6 \\) and \\( y = 10 \\) into the equations of the lines.\n\nFirst, substitute \\( x = 6 \\) and \\( y = 10 \\) into the equation \\( y = mx + 4 \\):\n\\[\n10 = m \\cdot 6 + 4\n\\]\nSolving for \\( m \\), we get:\n\\[\n10 = 6m + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n10 - 4 = 6m\n\\]\n\\[\n6 = 6m\n\\]\n\\[\nm = 1\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\( x = 6 \\) and \\( y = 10 \\) into the equation \\( y = 3x + b \\):\n\\[\n10 = 3 \\cdot 6 + b\n\\]\nSolving for \\( b \\), we get:\n\\[\n10 = 18 + b\n\\]\n\\[\n10 - 18 = b\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -8\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\( m = 1 \\) and \\( b = -8 \\), we can find the value of \\( b + m \\):\n\\[\nb + m = -8 + 1 = -7\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( b + m \\) is \\(\\boxed{-7}\\).",
